QUESTION: Implement ‘re’ module in python 

ALGORITHM:

1.Start
2.Import re module
3.Define a string containing text, number, and email
4.Use search() to find first match
5.Use findall() to extract all patterns
6.Use match() to check beginning of string
7.Use sub() to replace patterns
8.Use split() to divide string
9.Extract specific patterns (email, words)
10.Display all outputs
11.Stop

CODE:
import re

# Input string
text = "Hello Yukthi, your phone number is 9876543210 and email is yukthi123@gmail.com"

print("Original Text:")
print(text)

 SEARCH 

 Search for first occurrence of a 10-digit number

print("\nUsing search():")
search_result = re.search(r"\d{10}", text)
if search_result:
    print("Phone number found:", search_result.group())
else:
    print("No phone number found")

 FINDALL 

 Find all digits in the string
print("\nUsing findall():")
all_digits = re.findall(r"\d", text)
print("All digits:", all_digits)

 Find all words
words = re.findall(r"\w+", text)
print("All words:", words)

MATCH 

 Check if string starts with 'Hello'
print("\nUsing match():")
match_result = re.match(r"Hello", text)
if match_result:
    print("Text starts with 'Hello'")
else:
    print("No match at beginning")

 SUBSTITUTE

Replace digits with '*'

print("\nUsing sub():")
new_text = re.sub(r"\d", "*", text)
print("After replacing digits:", new_text)

# Replace email domain
email_changed = re.sub(r"gmail.com", "example.com", text)
print("After replacing domain:", email_changed)

SPLIT

 Split string by spaces

print("\nUsing split():")
split_text = re.split(r"\s", text)
print("Split words:", split_text)

 Split using comma

split_comma = re.split(r",", text)
print("Split using comma:", split_comma)

 EXTRA PATTERNS 

 Find email

print("\nExtract Email:")
email = re.search(r"\S+@\S+", text)
if email:
    print("Email found:", email.group())

 Find words starting with 'y'

print("\nWords starting with 'y':")
y_words = re.findall(r"\by\w*", text, re.IGNORECASE)
print(y_words)

